<p>Even if options are physically installed in the printer, they cannot 
 be used unless they are configured in the properties dialog box. After 
 installing or uninstalling options, always update the option configuration.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If bidirectional communication is operating between 
 the printer and computer, open the printer properties dialog box or click 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Update Now</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab to obtain updates on option configuration automatically.</p></li>
<li><p>When the <span class="Term-Soft">Automatically Update 
 Printer Information</span> check box is selected, you can obtain updates 
 on option configuration automatically, simply by opening the printer properties 
 dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>If bidirectional communication is not operating, 
 you must update option configuration manually.</p></li>
</ul>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If you do not 
 log on as a member of the Administrators or Power Users group, the settings 
 on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> tab are unavailable.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Available functions 
 differ depending on the printer or printer driver you are using.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2>Updating the Option Configuration Manually (When Bidirectional Communication 
 Is Not Operating)</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, open the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="2">
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Options</span> area, 
 select check boxes of the options installed.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Punch Unit:</span> 
 list, select the type of the punch unit that is installed.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Total Memory:</span> 
 list, select the size of the memory that is installed in the printer.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray Settings</span> 
 area, click the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Input Tray Settings...</span> 
 button to open the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> 
 list, select the input tray where the paper is loaded.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Size:</span> 
 list, select the size of the paper loaded.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type:</span> 
 list, select the type of paper loaded.</p></li>
<li><p>If the selected input tray is set as unavailable 
 for the Auto Tray Select function at the printer, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Do 
 not Use Auto Tray Select</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Position</span> 
 area, select the direction of the paper loaded.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Modify Input Tray/Paper 
 Size</span> button to update or add the information in <span class="Term-Soft">Input 
 Tray:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Size:</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Paper 
 Type: </span>to <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray Settings List:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>After configuring all paper trays, click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close the dialog box. </p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the 
 printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
